e which will add  stochasticity to  um  icm  okay so here is the summary  so  um  let me summarize actually  um all the search algorithms for csps  that we've encountered so first we  looked at backtracking search  so the strategy is to extend partial  assignments and then backtrack when we  get to  the complete assignment  the backtracking search is  exact  it computes the actual  maximum weight assignment it's the only  algorithm that we're considering that  does that in general  but the main problem is that the time  can be exponential  in the number of variables  then we looked at a beam search  which  extends also extends partial assignments  and here we're trading off accuracy for  time so this is approximate  it will only give you a  an okay solution  but it's linear in the number of  variables  and local search um we saw iterative  conditional modes which  does local search by choosing the best  value of a variable at each given time  um is a different strategy here we're  starting with complete assignments and  modifying them to make them better  so here it's also  approximate  but it's fast just like beam search  okay so that concludes this module

